  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The smallest prime number is \\(2\\), since \\(1\\) is not prime. Therefore, any choice divisible by \\(2\\) has the smallest possible prime factor.\n\nOnly \\(58\\) is even, and \\(58=2\\cdot29\\). All the other choices are odd, so none has \\(2\\) as a factor. The answer is \\(58\\), choice \\(C\\).",
